implementationPlan.description:
Verify the landed contracts first; no edits in this step. For each item in the task description, grep or Read the LANDED code and record the exact names, fields, limits and reason codes in the step note:
- tools/getContext.ts and context/contextPacket.ts (C01 packetManifest, packetBudgetChars);
- context/contextDelta.ts and getContext.ts (C06a/C06: basePacketId, contextEpoch, the delta shape, the contextDelta reasons);
- context/planReuse*.ts with claimNextTask.ts and getContext.ts (C07 planReuse);
- context/recipes/recipe.ts and tools/submitPlan.ts (C08: RECIPE_ACTOR, recipeInstance, RecipeDefinition, .moe/recipes.json);
- context/recipes/docsLiteralReplace.ts (C09 params.allowedPaths, inputs and reasons).
Document only what landed. Error handling: if a dependency's landed contract contradicts its plan, document the landed one and say so in the completion summary.

Verify once, fresh. Run the gate in an isolated Linux snapshot of HEAD, with only the two docs overlaid: native deps, MOE_* unset, Linux-only PATH (mem:gotcha-daemon-linux-snapshot-gate). The gate is `cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test`, which includes the doc-reading tests, and it must exit 0. Also run `npm run lint` at the root. Supply the npm test command, exit code and output tail to complete_task.

Self-review:
- every documented name greps in the code;
- no sentence implies approval, readiness or evidence;
- no activation is described as landed (the assessPostpatch call site, epoch stamping, providers in packets);
- the anchors and links resolve.
